WEBVTT

00:08.300 --> 00:11.110
It came out so cleanly!
Is this edible, too?

00:18.300 --> 00:19.990
There's so much!

00:20.220 --> 00:24.050
Lady Serafina... aren't you
fitting in a little too well?

00:40.940 --> 00:48.580
The Warrior Princess and the Barbaric King

01:57.470 --> 02:01.490
U-Um, Lady Serafina, might I have a word?

02:01.850 --> 02:04.140
What is it, Malcius?

02:04.140 --> 02:07.810
You said you intended on returning
to Illdoren someday, so...

02:08.320 --> 02:11.620
Should you really have
accepted that necklace?

02:15.860 --> 02:19.660
Probably not. I think I
may have made a mistake.

02:19.660 --> 02:24.400
Even if it has no binding power
under the Order of Commoneras,

02:24.400 --> 02:26.660
agreeing to an engagement
might have been a bit rash.

02:26.660 --> 02:29.560
But with what Resia told me...

02:29.560 --> 02:32.920
Even if she was once a princess,
she's the great chief's wife!

02:32.920 --> 02:35.670
You shouldn't have taken her at her word!

02:36.540 --> 02:38.170
Fear not, Malcius.

02:38.530 --> 02:44.510
I-I will never forget
my duty as a n-noble!

02:44.510 --> 02:46.560
That is not very convincing!

02:47.150 --> 02:48.840
I-It's just that...

02:48.840 --> 02:51.100
I was giving some thought
to what Resia said

02:51.100 --> 02:57.690
about searching for my own happiness,
or... something along those lines.

02:58.080 --> 03:01.700
And that's what made you so indecisive?

03:01.700 --> 03:05.260
I-Indecisive...?

03:05.650 --> 03:10.420
I realize that's the case...
I do, and yet...

03:10.770 --> 03:13.330
When I try to think about
what happiness means to me,

03:13.330 --> 03:15.750
after a life of nothing but
chivalry and swordplay...

03:17.460 --> 03:20.540
I'm at a loss! Nothing comes to mind!

03:21.620 --> 03:26.890
That's rather pitiful.
And I have to say...

03:28.910 --> 03:33.530
It's bizarre seeing the knight among
knights, Lavillant the Frozen,

03:33.530 --> 03:36.400
act like a naive village girl!

03:41.330 --> 03:44.120
Well, I can see why
you'd view me as such...

03:44.120 --> 03:47.450
but it's more like a misunderstanding.

03:48.160 --> 03:51.870
Before all this, all I had in my head
were my duty and the war.

03:53.330 --> 03:55.550
Fulfilling the duty of someone
 born into a noble house

03:55.550 --> 03:57.420
blessed with talent for war...

03:57.740 --> 04:01.260
For as long as I can remember,
those things have been my focus.

04:01.690 --> 04:02.930
That's...

04:03.440 --> 04:06.910
Thinking back, I may have
obsessed with those matters.

04:07.820 --> 04:09.610
Though I can see why you
might have interpreted

04:09.610 --> 04:11.390
that as behaving like the ideal knight.

04:13.040 --> 04:17.150
It's not that I resent
you for it. It's just...

04:17.670 --> 04:19.000
Since coming to this land,

04:19.000 --> 04:21.900
meeting its people,
and seeing how they live their lives...

04:22.670 --> 04:25.900
I may have been a knight commander
with the Eastern Expedition,

04:25.900 --> 04:30.420
but to them, I was little more
than an invader from the west.

04:31.910 --> 04:34.120
Lady Serafina...

04:34.120 --> 04:38.910
I wouldn't say that I regret the
last seven years of my life.

04:39.640 --> 04:43.510
I was doing what I believed,
at the time, was the right thing.

04:44.080 --> 04:50.810
But... I could've never imagined that
the people here wouldn't hate me for it.

04:51.550 --> 04:54.560
And you feel guilty because of it?

04:56.060 --> 05:01.070
Could that guilt truly drive
you to abandon your homeland?!

05:02.480 --> 05:03.480
My homeland...

05:03.990 --> 05:07.750
The desolate, barren lands of Illdoren.

05:07.750 --> 05:12.800
For all the gains that this expedition
has had over seven years,

05:12.800 --> 05:15.960
so many of our fighting men were slain...

05:16.280 --> 05:19.150
That I question whether it was worth it.

05:19.910 --> 05:21.450
Whether I attend to my homeland,

05:21.880 --> 05:25.290
or my guilt... either way, I would
be forsaking something I care about.

05:25.850 --> 05:29.590
I'm not sure I like the sound of that.

05:30.640 --> 05:34.740
Cersei? I can see why you would,
considering what you've been through.

05:35.260 --> 05:37.660
But even if the people
here pay it no mind,

05:37.660 --> 05:40.100
I can't simply forget
the things I've done.

05:40.530 --> 05:44.590
I can't forgot how my actions should
have earned me their distrust and hate.

05:44.590 --> 05:47.550
Oh, I'm done talking about that stuff.

05:48.450 --> 05:50.730
But for all your talk about
guilt and obligation,

05:50.730 --> 05:54.370
you're still wearing that
engagement necklace.

05:55.030 --> 05:58.250
Mulling over your misgivings while you're
wearing something that would come off

05:58.680 --> 06:02.540
if you wanted it to
is practically farcical.

06:06.510 --> 06:09.760
Besides, no matter what your worries
are, we all still need to eat.

06:10.110 --> 06:14.420
I'd say that's more pressing than
the things that are on your mind.

06:21.660 --> 06:26.580
Thinking back on it now, the food
in these lands is so abundant.

06:29.320 --> 06:33.540
The woods and waterways
are rich with nourishment.

06:33.540 --> 06:36.660
And the dragons in the forests,
ferocious though they are,

06:36.660 --> 06:41.180
are large enough to feed hundreds
of people after a single hunt.

06:41.180 --> 06:43.290
Yes, the woods.

06:43.700 --> 06:47.170
The woods here are deep,
and the mountains are rugged...

06:47.170 --> 06:50.180
It stands to reason that people
would be unable to farm such land.

06:50.780 --> 06:54.180
Without cultivating the land, there's no
room to live or any way to grow grain...

06:54.560 --> 06:57.310
But upon cultivating it, they risk losing
the land's bounty in the long term.

06:58.280 --> 07:02.050
It's been nearly 700 years of us trying
to claim their land, every few decades...

07:02.600 --> 07:04.710
Compared to our borders
before the expeditions,

07:04.710 --> 07:06.690
it's true that we have
claimed more territory,

07:06.690 --> 07:09.130
which should include fertile lands...

07:09.740 --> 07:11.140
But it makes little difference.

07:11.140 --> 07:12.770
Are we simply depleting it too quickly?

07:13.470 --> 07:14.390
Sera.

07:17.830 --> 07:22.560
I understand you're deep in thought,
but it's made you look like a squirrel.

07:23.830 --> 07:26.180
Here, Lady Serafina!

07:29.200 --> 07:31.090
Th-Thank you. What a relief.

07:31.090 --> 07:33.060
Are you all right, Sera?

07:34.940 --> 07:37.970
Were you thinking about the things
you mentioned this afternoon?

07:41.790 --> 07:46.250
No. I was pondering the significance of
the Eastern Expedition to the people,

07:46.250 --> 07:48.440
as both a knight and a noble.

07:48.900 --> 07:52.460
Seizing your lands for
the sake of our people...

07:53.520 --> 07:58.230
I cannot say with confidence that
it was a righteous cause anymore.

07:59.030 --> 08:00.360
But were I to say that,

08:00.700 --> 08:03.160
would the knights and soldiers
who fought resent me?

08:03.160 --> 08:05.700
Would the citizens, who were
saved by our expansion?

08:07.280 --> 08:08.220
Sera.

08:09.960 --> 08:13.510
After we finish eating,
why don't we talk outside?

08:16.130 --> 08:18.080
The beauty of the triplet
moons remains the same,

08:18.080 --> 08:20.520
whether in the east or the west.

08:20.810 --> 08:23.970
Indeed. They're beautiful, Sera.

08:23.970 --> 08:24.800
Yes.

08:26.210 --> 08:31.250
My pondering from this afternoon,
and over the past few days...

08:31.250 --> 08:33.270
I genuinely don't know what to do anymore.

08:34.160 --> 08:36.030
Part of me thinks I should return

08:36.030 --> 08:38.930
for the sake of my people 
and my comrades...

08:38.930 --> 08:42.410
While another wants to
consider my own happiness.

08:42.840 --> 08:45.710
And it feels like I'm at a crossroads.

08:47.050 --> 08:52.430
In that case, perhaps...
you could use your imagination.

08:52.430 --> 08:53.800
Imagination?

08:55.290 --> 08:59.220
That's not the kind of thing
I'd expect to hear from you.

08:59.220 --> 09:01.180
I don't see why.

09:01.180 --> 09:03.120
I'd say, compared to most,

09:03.120 --> 09:06.940
I give a fair bit more thought
to things like dreams and ideals.

09:07.250 --> 09:11.560
The Tefyu say that having 
a strong enough desire

09:11.560 --> 09:15.700
can make a wish reality.

09:15.700 --> 09:19.530
If they're right, then I imagine
doubts can only give rise to regrets.

09:19.870 --> 09:24.860
Which is why, Sera, it may help you
to imagine what the outcomes might be,

09:24.860 --> 09:26.380
in order to decide what you want.

09:26.820 --> 09:30.210
Imagination... Imagining things, eh?

09:31.710 --> 09:36.820
Supposing I return home with some
sort of positive accomplishment...

09:40.620 --> 09:42.780
More than anything,
I'd want our people to not starve,

09:42.780 --> 09:46.620
and enjoy great bounty. Enough to
put an end to the expeditions...

09:46.620 --> 09:48.290
But even should that happen,

09:48.290 --> 09:52.320
I'll likely meet a dour fate as a noble
after being taken captive.

09:52.320 --> 09:55.490
Locked away in some chamber
for the rest of my days...

09:55.710 --> 09:58.990
The more I think about it,
the more grim it seems.

10:01.050 --> 10:04.490
Granted, I knew that was a possibility...

10:04.980 --> 10:08.000
But now, suppose, hypothetically,

10:08.470 --> 10:13.130
I abandon my duties as a knight
and choose Veor instead...

10:13.930 --> 10:16.510
Rustic as he is, I wouldn't
say he's vulgar or anything.

10:16.510 --> 10:19.080
And his skill with a sword,
while not a match for mine,

10:19.080 --> 10:20.980
is a near contest thanks
to his strength and size...

10:22.760 --> 10:24.700
Then again, he's only 18...

10:25.110 --> 10:27.520
with experience, he may yet
become stronger than me.

10:27.860 --> 10:31.240
And as Resia's son, his heritage
is without question...

10:32.270 --> 10:36.810
Hard as it is to imagine,
suppose we had a child?

10:36.810 --> 10:40.630
A child?! Could Veor and
I have a child together?!

10:40.950 --> 10:43.350
I suppose we could.

10:43.710 --> 10:46.420
Huh, that might not be so bad...

10:50.280 --> 10:52.840
Wait, this is more like fantasizing!

10:54.030 --> 10:57.260
And I'm no closer to making a decision!

10:57.260 --> 11:00.030
I see. You're unsure of what to do, then.

11:01.200 --> 11:06.800
I had honestly expected that
you'd be more keen to reject me.

11:07.240 --> 11:10.280
Which is why I'm pleased
to see your indecision.

11:11.830 --> 11:16.010
It means that your feelings for me are
comparable to your previous way of life,

11:16.010 --> 11:20.070
your beliefs, and your pride, does it not?

11:21.790 --> 11:24.830
Which is plenty for me, at the moment.

11:25.270 --> 11:27.080
Do you realize...

11:27.080 --> 11:30.020
that you're contradicting
what you said before?

11:30.020 --> 11:33.050
First you tell me not to hesitate,
and then to ponder more...

11:33.050 --> 11:36.820
Well, the problem is yours to solve, Sera.

11:36.820 --> 11:39.590
All I can really do is be by your side.

11:39.590 --> 11:44.850
That said... it may be wise for
you to broaden your perspective

11:44.850 --> 11:47.350
if you wish to resolve your problem.

11:48.040 --> 11:49.100
How's that?

11:49.670 --> 11:52.790
Perhaps it's time you
consider taking a journey.

11:55.130 --> 11:56.420
Lord Sidius.

11:56.420 --> 11:57.920
Your humble servant, Hilbane,

11:57.920 --> 12:00.740
has returned from
the expedition with news.

12:01.010 --> 12:05.620
I beg your pardon for coming unannounced,
as it is of an urgent nature.

12:06.380 --> 12:07.220
Enter.

12:07.670 --> 12:08.410
Yes, sir.

12:16.640 --> 12:19.630
First, let me to praise you
for returning with this news.

12:20.190 --> 12:22.100
The fact that you're here
makes the nature

12:22.100 --> 12:24.890
of this information somewhat obvious.

12:25.400 --> 12:27.490
Has Serafina fallen in battle?

12:28.270 --> 12:32.750
N-No, sir. Her remains were never found.

12:32.750 --> 12:35.670
It's likely that, while battling

12:35.670 --> 12:39.030
an enemy general as our rear guard,
she was taken captive.

12:40.020 --> 12:41.440
A distinction without a difference.

12:41.990 --> 12:43.030
Yes, sir.

12:43.030 --> 12:44.730
The matter of my sister can wait.

12:44.730 --> 12:48.080
What of the remaining strength
of the expedition's forces?

12:48.080 --> 12:53.540
Sir! Thanks to the princess' efforts,
our losses were light.

12:55.560 --> 13:01.050
Light losses. It won't take long before
another expedition is organized, then.

13:02.100 --> 13:04.420
A genuinely perplexing problem.

13:06.490 --> 13:07.980
Did she not realize that

13:07.980 --> 13:11.300
sacrificing her own life would
not suffice to save the people?

13:12.690 --> 13:14.730
My poor Serafina.

13:21.620 --> 13:24.150
A trip... a journey to
a distant place, eh?

13:24.890 --> 13:28.730
I can't deny it's a perfect opportunity
to expand my perspective.

13:29.920 --> 13:33.700
But where will we be going?

13:35.010 --> 13:38.170
Perhaps the elegant
capital of the elves...

13:38.620 --> 13:42.170
Or the paradise where the fairies frolic?

13:42.450 --> 13:45.920
The dryads... or rather,
those living plants...

13:45.920 --> 13:49.680
It's odd how easily my mind comes
up with these bizarre images.

13:49.960 --> 13:54.680
I wonder if the dwarves have an
expansive, subterranean kingdom.

13:54.680 --> 13:59.250
Oh, that can't be!
This isn't some fantasy novel!

13:59.670 --> 14:00.530
Sera.

14:01.910 --> 14:04.410
You're interested in the
Quefto's settlement?

14:04.410 --> 14:07.650
Veor! Don't scare me like that!
You're liable to give me a heart attack.

14:08.250 --> 14:09.630
Forgive me, forgive me.

14:09.630 --> 14:14.330
But their settlement is actually
close to what you described.

14:15.110 --> 14:17.820
While the underground buildings
leave an impression,

14:17.820 --> 14:22.460
the most striking thing is
that they have hot springs!

14:24.150 --> 14:25.350
And what is that?

14:25.910 --> 14:28.530
I suppose it's not clear
from the words alone...

14:29.020 --> 14:34.070
And someone born in a land of only
plains would have know way of knowing.

14:34.070 --> 14:36.730
So, what exactly is a hot spring?

14:37.660 --> 14:40.250
How to describe it... let's see...

14:41.050 --> 14:44.230
Think of it as a natural hot bath.

14:45.030 --> 14:46.870
A hot bath? In nature?

14:46.870 --> 14:50.950
Come now! Hot baths are a luxury
for those with the time and money

14:50.950 --> 14:52.370
for a great deal of firewood.

14:52.370 --> 14:55.070
According to the Quefto,
this water is hot to begin with.

14:55.070 --> 14:56.870
Something to do with heat from the ground.

15:00.990 --> 15:04.760
They just... have hot water from out of
nowhere?! Does that seem fair to you?!

15:04.760 --> 15:07.440
The lakeside village is has
plenty of water and dragon meat,

15:07.440 --> 15:09.760
to say nothing of lumber!

15:09.760 --> 15:11.350
And now I find out the
dwarves have mythril

15:11.350 --> 15:13.650
and an infinite source of hot water!

15:13.650 --> 15:17.270
How in the blazes are these
lands so bloody rich?!

15:17.270 --> 15:20.150
I'm glad to see this sort of
thing still surprises you.

15:20.150 --> 15:24.380
Granted, the hot springs
came as a shock to me, too.

15:24.810 --> 15:28.240
I can only remember my time
from the frontier village...

15:28.240 --> 15:31.160
But the memories I have of
bathing in the river in winter

15:31.160 --> 15:33.410
make it clear to me how
valuable fuel for fire can be.

15:34.010 --> 15:37.150
The outskirts of the wilderness
that the west have colonized

15:37.150 --> 15:41.450
aren't that much better than the relative
best parts of Illdoren territory.

15:41.450 --> 15:44.670
The lack of dragons and
fairies is proof of that.

15:44.960 --> 15:46.090
True enough.

15:46.840 --> 15:51.370
Not that I'd want to live
any place with those things.

15:51.370 --> 15:55.300
I honestly still can't understand how
it doesn't bother you barbarians.

15:56.480 --> 15:58.850
Do you really think it's that simple?

16:00.330 --> 16:04.430
The warriors here have no real option
but to hunt dragons in order to survive.

16:04.740 --> 16:08.250
Those incapable of that kind
of lifestyle end up dying.

16:09.770 --> 16:12.290
Villages without healthy warriors

16:12.290 --> 16:15.320
often end up becoming feeding
grounds for dragons.

16:15.650 --> 16:16.970
That's...

16:17.550 --> 16:19.330
It is what it is.

16:19.610 --> 16:23.520
Either cultivate a barren land where
 your meager harvests are taken as taxes

16:23.520 --> 16:25.970
and risk freezing and starvation...

16:25.970 --> 16:29.470
or live someplace where
 you can eat your fill

16:29.470 --> 16:31.840
but will die without the
protection of strong fighters.

16:34.300 --> 16:38.830
All I can say for certain is
that we will die someday.

16:38.830 --> 16:43.600
And I would personally rather be eaten
by a dragon than starve to death.

16:43.600 --> 16:46.950
Doesn't being part of the
circle of life at least

16:46.950 --> 16:49.760
feel like a death with a purpose?

16:52.080 --> 16:54.360
I can't understand what
you're saying at all.

16:54.600 --> 16:58.430
That makes sense. Chalk it
up to a difference in values.

16:58.430 --> 17:03.480
I-I mean, if you're eaten, there's no
last rites or burial! It's so uncivilized!

17:03.480 --> 17:05.930
That's just not as much
of a concern here.

17:08.440 --> 17:13.320
You actually asked the dwarf
craftsmen to make me a helmet?!

17:13.320 --> 17:14.380
Yes.

17:14.380 --> 17:18.640
But how am I to pay?
I can't access my assets from here.

17:18.640 --> 17:21.320
There's no need to worry about that.

17:21.320 --> 17:25.160
The Morisuberi we hunted the other day
was more than enough to pay for it.

17:25.160 --> 17:28.900
Since you struck the killing blow,
the biggest portion of it was yours.

17:28.900 --> 17:33.260
Add to that my portion, as well as your
reward for striking down the Fiend.

17:33.650 --> 17:38.390
Elder Balhath said he was going
to make you something in mythril.

17:38.390 --> 17:40.410
Look forward to it.

17:42.220 --> 17:43.810
That sounds amazing!

17:46.710 --> 17:48.760
She seems thrilled.

17:49.090 --> 17:53.170
I've never seen Lady Serafina so happy...

17:53.620 --> 17:56.220
When shall we go, then?
When will it be ready?

17:57.130 --> 18:01.040
I'll have to ask. Could the
three of you cover your ears?

18:04.110 --> 18:08.300
Lady Vyufmec!

18:12.940 --> 18:16.270
"Thundering Voice" never stops
being an apt description.

18:20.800 --> 18:24.890
That was a nice bit of Thundering Voice,
Orkfiem! Plenty of willpower!

18:24.890 --> 18:27.580
And it's good to see you again, Illdoren!

18:27.580 --> 18:29.530
So energetic...

18:29.530 --> 18:32.540
Sorry to call upon you so
suddenly, Lady Vyufmec.

18:32.540 --> 18:37.360
Don't be! Any request from Orkfiem
is a top priority for us.

18:37.360 --> 18:40.090
So, you've got a message
you need delivered?

18:41.310 --> 18:46.690
To the Kurogane Mountains, in the
settlement with the most Quefto.

18:46.690 --> 18:50.510
From Orkfiem to Elder Balhath:

18:50.510 --> 18:54.000
I'd like to know when the
item I ordered will be ready.

18:54.000 --> 18:56.990
Got it! And I'm off!

18:58.260 --> 18:59.580
She vanished again.

18:59.580 --> 19:03.150
Wind Tefyu exist in all places at once.

19:03.150 --> 19:05.050
Call upon them with
 willpower in your voice,

19:05.050 --> 19:06.380
and they'll come to your aid.

19:06.730 --> 19:10.320
Granted, only Father and I
can manage that these days.

19:12.780 --> 19:16.280
Huh, it occurs to me that
as the next great chief,

19:16.280 --> 19:19.030
do you mediate negotiations
between the other clans?

19:19.030 --> 19:20.350
That I do.

19:20.350 --> 19:23.320
I'd even say that's the majority
of the alliance's leader's duties.

19:23.320 --> 19:26.370
Along with hunting Fiends, acting as
the linchpin of the great cleansing,

19:26.370 --> 19:30.260
and dividing various gains between
the clans so everyone is happy...

19:30.260 --> 19:32.830
That last bit is particularly tough.

19:32.830 --> 19:34.850
For all your wild looks,

19:34.850 --> 19:36.890
you've got no shortage of
responsibility, do you?

19:37.340 --> 19:38.500
That I don't.

19:39.120 --> 19:42.610
But I only intend to do what I can.

19:42.610 --> 19:47.620
That's all any of us can do,
ultimately, as we live out our lives.

19:47.620 --> 19:49.080
It might be a heavy burden,

19:49.080 --> 19:52.420
but I take pride in inheriting
it from my forefathers, Sera.

19:53.000 --> 19:54.240
Veor...

19:54.850 --> 19:58.090
I thought you so uncivilized
when we first met,

19:58.090 --> 20:00.800
but your royal blood has
never been more obvious.

20:01.900 --> 20:03.660
Have you fallen in
love with me all over again?

20:03.660 --> 20:06.260
Wh-What...?! What do you mean again?!

20:07.090 --> 20:10.050
Come now, it's just a turn of phrase!

20:10.050 --> 20:13.940
A-As a noble, it does make me see
you in a different light, though...

20:14.820 --> 20:18.800
I'm back!
Huh? Why're you so red, Illdoren?

20:18.800 --> 20:23.690
I-It's nothing! Now what was
the reply to the message?

20:23.690 --> 20:25.770
Oh, that! Right, right.

20:25.770 --> 20:30.660
"Balhath to Orkfiem: It'll be
ready tomorrow morning!" he says.

20:30.660 --> 20:34.040
That is excellent!
And it settles things, Sera.

20:34.830 --> 20:38.240
Your journey to expand
your horizons will begin

20:38.240 --> 20:40.840
with a trip to a Quefto settlement!

20:41.720 --> 20:42.630
Right!

20:49.850 --> 20:52.310
Translation: Lee Francis

Timing: Andy Ellis

Editing: Zachary Carlysle

Quality Control: Salem Alabanza

Translation Check: Sho Stifler

20:54.290 --> 20:56.810
What a refreshing morning!

20:57.630 --> 21:00.500
Still, leaving while fully armored...

21:00.500 --> 21:03.320
how likely is it we'll have
to fight once we get there?

21:03.320 --> 21:06.820
More that we can't let our guard down
until we reach the Quefto settlement.

21:07.500 --> 21:10.730
Take a half step out of human
territory, and the dragons reign.

21:10.730 --> 21:12.910
Better safe than sorry, no?

21:13.230 --> 21:16.770
Now then, our destination
is the Kurogane Mountains.

21:16.770 --> 21:19.590
Near the foot of that biggest peak,
hidden by the closer one.

21:19.590 --> 21:22.190
The biggest mountain,
behind the other...?

21:22.190 --> 21:25.590
I had wondered where
exactly we were going,

21:26.290 --> 21:29.660
but we can't possibly cover
that distance in one day!

21:29.660 --> 21:32.360
Who's to say how long it might take?

21:33.810 --> 21:35.850
And I'd say you're worried about nothing.

21:36.210 --> 21:38.850
Now, bear witness!

21:38.850 --> 21:41.960
Among the many Cornem settlements,

21:41.960 --> 21:44.860
this secret is only taught to
those of the Lakeside Village!

21:45.290 --> 21:47.860
The symbol of our esteem
for the dragons that soar!

21:50.880 --> 21:52.120
What is this?!

21:53.260 --> 21:57.120
It is the dream of us warriors
who don the armor of dragons!

21:57.120 --> 22:01.170
The reverence of our ancestors
takes the form of a beast,

22:01.170 --> 22:02.970
growing until it takes spirit form...

22:03.630 --> 22:06.150
Becoming an Echo Dragon!

22:13.890 --> 22:15.100
We're flying!

22:25.650 --> 22:30.520
Sera. Does this demonstrate our
reverence for the dragons sufficiently?

22:30.520 --> 22:33.660
You won't find much that is as
thrilling as flying through the sky!

22:33.660 --> 22:36.160
Y-Yeah! How could it not?!

22:37.210 --> 22:38.160
I see!

22:41.390 --> 22:44.020
You two seem more and more like newlyweds.

22:44.550 --> 22:48.270
C-Cersei! Veor and I are...

22:48.270 --> 22:50.180
Do we really seem that way?!

22:50.180 --> 22:52.180
Why? Does it bother you?

22:56.180 --> 22:58.180
No, it does not.

22:58.470 --> 23:00.060
Are you that fond of him?!

23:05.420 --> 23:07.990
Hold on tight, everyone!

23:16.520 --> 23:17.560
Are we under attack?

23:17.560 --> 23:19.620
But where did that flame come from?

23:19.980 --> 23:22.420
We've caught the ire of a troublesome foe.

23:22.420 --> 23:25.000
There is only one type of
dragon that breathes fire.

23:25.320 --> 23:28.010
The masters of the Kurogane Mountains...

23:32.760 --> 23:37.060
The fire dragons—a strain of
true dragons—the Guren Nairi!
